cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AI Voiceover Studio in your work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "AI Voiceover Studio"
abstract: >-
  An open-source Python CLI and library that turns a Markdown script into an AI voiceover
  (text to speech), SRT subtitles and a captioned faceless video for YouTube, Shorts, Reels
  and TikTok, with B-roll per paragraph, word-by-word animated captions and background music
  ducked under the voice. Works with free Microsoft Edge neural voices; OpenAI and Miragea
  (voice cloning) are optional engines.
authors:
  - name: "Miragea contributors"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-11-07"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yanghhu/ai-voiceover-studio"
url: "https://github.com/yanghhu/ai-voiceover-studio#readme"
keywords:
  - ai voiceover
  - text to speech
  - faceless youtube
  - word-by-word subtitles
  - tiktok captions
  - text to video
  - subtitles
  - python cli
